{"version":"1.4","group":"V401","entries":[{"id":"learn:02654355-v","headword":"perpetuate","group":"V401","partOfSpeech":"verb","itemIds":["JBKROW013564","JBKROW016925"],"localGlosses":["영속화하다"],"definitionEn":"cause to continue or prevail","definitionKo":"계속 이어지거나 널리 남도록 만들다","memoryKo":"이미 생긴 현상을 반복해 계속 살아남게 하는 모습을 기억하세요.","usageKo":"관습, 오해, 불평등처럼 어떤 상태가 반복을 통해 계속되게 만드는 문맥에 자주 씁니다.","examTrapKo":"즉시 영원하게 만든다는 뜻보다 기존 상태를 계속 이어지게 한다는 뜻으로 읽어야 합니다.","contrasts":[{"word":"preserve","noteKo":"preserve는 손상·소멸하지 않도록 보호함을, perpetuate는 반복하거나 전승해 계속 존재하게 함을 강조합니다."}],"example":{"en":"Repeating the rumor will perpetuate the harm.","ko":"그 소문을 반복하면 피해가 계속될 것이다.","kind":"editorial"},"nuance":{},"sources":[{"name":"Open English WordNet","url":"https://en-word.net/downloads/english-wordnet-2025-json.zip","license":"CC BY 4.0","edition":"2025","attribution":"Princeton WordNet; Open English WordNet Team"},{"name":"Wiktionary via Kaikki","url":"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/English/meaning/p/pe/perpetuate.jsonl","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0 and GFDL","edition":"checked 2026-09-04"}],"verification":{"status":"cross-agreed","reviewer":"Codex editorial cross-check","checkedAtKst":"2026.09.04","evidence":[{"source":"Open English WordNet 2025","independenceGroup":"WordNet","url":"https://en-word.net/downloads/english-wordnet-2025-json.zip","result":"agree","contentSha256":"7d749f6e2c39e6970e4997839dcf6e42fd281f3c2fae0171d2192bae8cfa4b51"},{"source":"Wiktionary via Kaikki","independenceGroup":"Wiktionary","url":"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/English/meaning/p/pe/perpetuate.jsonl","result":"agree","contentSha256":"4d622c2222054d569794ae47f7d94bdf19015b5567745391a7a4e7f4dffc5d3a"}]}},{"id":"learn:10574739-n","headword":"scapegoat","group":"V401","partOfSpeech":"noun","itemIds":["JBKROW001793","JBKROW003687","JBKROW013575","JBKROW017196","JBKROW018140","JBKROW018724","JBKROW022130"],"localGlosses":["희생양"],"definitionEn":"someone who is punished for the errors of others","definitionKo":"다른 사람들의 잘못 때문에 대신 벌을 받는 사람","memoryKo":"잘못은 다른 사람이 했지만 책임과 벌은 희생양에게 몰리는 장면을 떠올리세요.","usageKo":"조직이나 사회가 실패의 진짜 원인 대신 특정 개인이나 집단에 책임을 전가하는 문맥에 씁니다.","examTrapKo":"실제 잘못을 저지른 culprit가 아니라 부당하게 책임을 떠안은 대상입니다.","contrasts":[{"word":"culprit","noteKo":"culprit는 실제 잘못의 책임자이고, scapegoat는 남의 잘못까지 부당하게 뒤집어쓴 대상입니다."}],"example":{"en":"The manager made the intern a scapegoat for the failure.","ko":"관리자는 그 실패의 책임을 인턴에게 희생양처럼 떠넘겼다.","kind":"editorial"},"nuance":{},"sources":[{"name":"Open English WordNet","url":"https://en-word.net/downloads/english-wordnet-2025-json.zip","license":"CC BY 4.0","edition":"2025","attribution":"Princeton WordNet; Open English WordNet Team"},{"name":"Wiktionary via Kaikki","url":"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/English/meaning/s/sc/scapegoat.jsonl","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0 and GFDL","edition":"checked 2026-09-04"}],"verification":{"status":"cross-agreed","reviewer":"Codex editorial cross-check","checkedAtKst":"2026.09.04","evidence":[{"source":"Open English WordNet 2025","independenceGroup":"WordNet","url":"https://en-word.net/downloads/english-wordnet-2025-json.zip","result":"agree","contentSha256":"7d749f6e2c39e6970e4997839dcf6e42fd281f3c2fae0171d2192bae8cfa4b51"},{"source":"Wiktionary via Kaikki","independenceGroup":"Wiktionary","url":"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/English/meaning/s/sc/scapegoat.jsonl","result":"agree","contentSha256":"0077272c2afa397b98cba346cc38ce0f5df3b345ca28884e6aebd0e9480cf4d6"}]},"audio":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/5/5e/En-us-scapegoat.ogg/En-us-scapegoat.ogg.mp3","region":"US","source":"Wikimedia Commons","sourcePage":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:En-us-scapegoat.ogg","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","attribution":"Dvortygirl"}},{"id":"learn:00177411-a","headword":"auspicious","group":"V401","partOfSpeech":"adjective","itemIds":["JBKROW004315","JBKROW006336","JBKROW013593","JBKROW015766","JBKROW017550"],"localGlosses":["길조(吉兆)의, 상서로운"],"definitionEn":"auguring favorable circumstances and good luck","definitionKo":"유리한 상황과 행운을 예고하는","memoryKo":"앞으로 일이 잘 풀릴 것임을 알려 주는 좋은 징조를 떠올리세요.","usageKo":"시작, 날, 신호 등이 미래의 성공이나 행운을 암시하는 문맥에 씁니다.","examTrapKo":"이미 운이 좋았다는 fortunate와 달리 앞으로의 좋은 결과를 예고한다는 뜻이 핵심입니다.","contrasts":[{"word":"fortunate","noteKo":"fortunate는 실제로 행운을 얻은 상태를, auspicious는 미래 성공을 암시하는 좋은 징조나 조건을 나타냅니다."}],"example":{"en":"The clear morning was an auspicious start to the journey.","ko":"맑은 아침은 여행의 길한 출발을 알렸다.","kind":"editorial"},"nuance":{},"sources":[{"name":"Open English WordNet","url":"https://en-word.net/downloads/english-wordnet-2025-json.zip","license":"CC BY 4.0","edition":"2025","attribution":"Princeton WordNet; Open English WordNet Team"},{"name":"Wiktionary via Kaikki","url":"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/English/meaning/a/au/auspicious.jsonl","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0 and GFDL","edition":"checked 2026-09-04"}],"verification":{"status":"cross-agreed","reviewer":"Codex editorial cross-check","checkedAtKst":"2026.09.04","evidence":[{"source":"Open English WordNet 2025","independenceGroup":"WordNet","url":"https://en-word.net/downloads/english-wordnet-2025-json.zip","result":"agree","contentSha256":"7d749f6e2c39e6970e4997839dcf6e42fd281f3c2fae0171d2192bae8cfa4b51"},{"source":"Wiktionary via Kaikki","independenceGroup":"Wiktionary","url":"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/English/meaning/a/au/auspicious.jsonl","result":"agree","contentSha256":"00fbc74b4bdd756f394bc2bcc3337e442077898fe5d6b2309ec1591614211080"}]},"audio":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/e/e2/En-us-auspicious.ogg/En-us-auspicious.ogg.mp3","region":"US","source":"Wikimedia Commons","sourcePage":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:En-us-auspicious.ogg","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","attribution":"Neskaya"}},{"id":"learn:02186120-s","headword":"intricate","group":"V401","partOfSpeech":"adjective","itemIds":["JBKROW004867","JBKROW007274","JBKROW013637","JBKROW014053","JBKROW016641"],"localGlosses":["복잡한"],"definitionEn":"having many complexly arranged elements; elaborate","definitionKo":"복잡하게 배열된 요소가 많이 있는, 정교한","memoryKo":"여러 가닥과 세부 요소가 촘촘히 얽힌 구조를 떠올리세요.","usageKo":"무늬, 기계, 계획, 논증처럼 세부 요소가 정교하고 복잡하게 연결된 대상을 설명할 때 씁니다.","examTrapKo":"단지 어렵다는 뜻이 아니라 많은 세부 요소가 서로 복잡하게 얽혀 있다는 구조적 의미가 중심입니다.","contrasts":[{"word":"complicated","noteKo":"complicated는 이해·해결하기 어려움을 넓게 뜻하고, intricate는 세부 요소가 정교하게 얽힌 구조를 강조합니다."}],"example":{"en":"The machine contains an intricate network of gears.","ko":"그 기계에는 톱니바퀴가 정교하게 얽힌 구조가 들어 있다.","kind":"editorial"},"nuance":{},"sources":[{"name":"Open English WordNet","url":"https://en-word.net/downloads/english-wordnet-2025-json.zip","license":"CC BY 4.0","edition":"2025","attribution":"Princeton WordNet; Open English WordNet Team"},{"name":"Wiktionary via Kaikki","url":"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/English/meaning/i/in/intricate.jsonl","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0 and GFDL","edition":"checked 2026-09-04"}],"verification":{"status":"cross-agreed","reviewer":"Codex editorial cross-check","checkedAtKst":"2026.09.04","evidence":[{"source":"Open English WordNet 2025","independenceGroup":"WordNet","url":"https://en-word.net/downloads/english-wordnet-2025-json.zip","result":"agree","contentSha256":"7d749f6e2c39e6970e4997839dcf6e42fd281f3c2fae0171d2192bae8cfa4b51"},{"source":"Wiktionary via Kaikki","independenceGroup":"Wiktionary","url":"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/English/meaning/i/in/intricate.jsonl","result":"agree","contentSha256":"74bb256e1c2a9ba9944506ba2070fa65719bffd16960a990128ee27261770cd2"}]},"audio":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/7/70/En-us-intricate.ogg/En-us-intricate.ogg.mp3","region":"US","source":"Wikimedia Commons","sourcePage":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:En-us-intricate.ogg","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","attribution":"Dvortygirl"}},{"id":"learn:04759785-n","headword":"disparity","group":"V401","partOfSpeech":"noun","itemIds":["JBKROW013639","JBKROW016149"],"localGlosses":["불균형; 불일치"],"definitionEn":"inequality or difference in some respect","definitionKo":"어떤 측면에서의 불평등이나 차이","memoryKo":"두 대상을 나란히 비교했을 때 크게 벌어진 격차를 떠올리세요.","usageKo":"소득, 기회, 수치, 대우처럼 비교 가능한 대상 사이의 불균형이나 격차를 나타낼 때 씁니다.","examTrapKo":"사실들이 서로 맞지 않는 discrepancy보다 두 집단이나 수준 사이의 불평등한 격차에 초점이 있습니다.","contrasts":[{"word":"discrepancy","noteKo":"discrepancy는 진술·수치가 서로 맞지 않음을, disparity는 양·수준·대우가 불평등하게 차이 남을 강조합니다."}],"example":{"en":"The report revealed a large disparity in income.","ko":"그 보고서는 소득의 큰 격차를 드러냈다.","kind":"editorial"},"nuance":{},"sources":[{"name":"Open English WordNet","url":"https://en-word.net/downloads/english-wordnet-2025-json.zip","license":"CC BY 4.0","edition":"2025","attribution":"Princeton WordNet; Open English WordNet Team"},{"name":"Wiktionary via Kaikki","url":"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/English/meaning/d/di/disparity.jsonl","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0 and GFDL","edition":"checked 2026-09-04"}],"verification":{"status":"cross-agreed","reviewer":"Codex editorial cross-check","checkedAtKst":"2026.09.04","evidence":[{"source":"Open English WordNet 2025","independenceGroup":"WordNet","url":"https://en-word.net/downloads/english-wordnet-2025-json.zip","result":"agree","contentSha256":"7d749f6e2c39e6970e4997839dcf6e42fd281f3c2fae0171d2192bae8cfa4b51"},{"source":"Wiktionary via Kaikki","independenceGroup":"Wiktionary","url":"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/English/meaning/d/di/disparity.jsonl","result":"agree","contentSha256":"6d4fd2332373595c226ffd49cc248ab90d771788b991639e3439d229d1b66ef5"}]}}]}
